, accuracy \u00b10.005\" -> /services", "Bending and welding departments -> /about", "MIG/TIG welding -> /services", "Sand blasting with 40 hp compressor -> /about", "Powder coating booth 7x21x7 ft -> /about", "In-house drafters for 3D design -> /services", "Industries: medical bed frames, carts, wheelchair frames -> /", "Industries: exercise equipment, food processing, architectural, construction -> /", "Industries: off-road/ATV, signage, furniture, industrial equipment -> /", "Industries: playground, automotive roll cages, retail fixtures -> /", "Commitment to on-time delivery of quality products -> /about", "One of Nevada''s only CNC tube lasers -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We fabricate from paper prints or electronic files, and work with the full range of raw materials: steel, stainless steel and aluminum sheet, tube, angle and channel, copper sheet and bar; and spring steel.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='nevada-precision-sheet-metal' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New Berlin Plastics was founded in 1975 by William Aukofer and Robert Zeman in New Berlin, Wisconsin. After relocations in 1976 and 1982, the company moved into a 100,000-square-foot facility in 1998 that serves as its corporate headquarters and manufacturing site. In July 2001, Jeffery Held and Mark Siewert acquired the business and have since directed its growth.

The company specializes in custom plastic injection molding, with a focus on scientific injection molding, medical device components, engineered plastic parts, and precision molded products for OEMs across Wisconsin and North America. Operations run from the 100,000-square-foot plant, supplemented by a recently acquired second building to meet rising demand. The firm emphasizes automation, mold flow analysis, and design-for-manufacturability support, and manages over 100 simultaneous customer projects through its proprietary LaunchLogic program.

New Berlin Plastics serves a diverse set of industries, including electrical utility, automotive and transportation, specialty hand and power tools, power sports, water treatment, building and construction, controls, healthcare and medical devices, lawn and garden, industrial, pet care, marine, and small engine. Customers are primarily OEMs that value high-quality engineered components and supply-chain reliability.

The company differentiates itself through tightly controlled scientific molding processes, a 99.8% customer acceptance rate, a 2.2% internal scrap rate, and a 98% on-time launch track record via LaunchLogic. Automation integration and comprehensive value-added services — from resin selection to tool transfer — are cited as core strengths.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Scientific injection molding", "Molding automation", "Mold flow analysis", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Resin selection", "Tool design", "Program management (LaunchLogic)", "Transfer tooling", "Material management", "Seminar and training services"], "industries": ["Electrical Utility", "Automotive & Transportation", "Specialty Hand & Power Tool", "Power Sports", "Water Treatment", "Building & Construction", "Controls", "Healthcare & Medical Devices", "Lawn & Garden", "Industrial", "Pet Care", "Marine", "Small Engine"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["99.8% customer acceptance rate on delivered parts", "2.2% internal scrap rate", "98% on-time launch track record via LaunchLogic process", "Scientific injection molding with tightly controlled, repeatable processes"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1975 by William Aukofer and Robert Zeman -> db", "100,000 sq ft facility in 1998 -> db", "Acquired July 2001 by Jeffery Held and Mark Siewert -> db", "99.8% customer acceptance rate -> /", "2.2% internal scrap rate -> /", "98% on-time launch track record via LaunchLogic -> /", "Over 100 simultaneous open customer projects -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /, /about-us", "Industries served list -> /, /about-us", "LaunchLogic proprietary process -> /, /services", "Scientific injection molding focus -> /", "Molding automation -> /", "Mold flow analysis -> /, /services", "Design assistance/DFM -> /, /services", "Resin selection -> /services", "Tool design -> /services", "Transfer tooling -> /services", "Material management -> /services", "Seminars/training -> /services", "New building (Building 2) purchased -> /", "Leadership team names -> /, /about-us", "UL certification support familiarity -> /, /about-us", "Customer quote ''key part of our supply chain'' -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "New Berlin Plastics is a custom plastic injection molding manufacturer specializing in scientific injection molding, medical device components, engineered plastic parts, and precision injection molded products for OEMs throughout Wisconsin and North America.", "founded_year": "1975", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-berlin-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New Jersey Semiconductor Products Inc. was established in 1957 and is headquartered in Springfield, New Jersey. The company operates from a two-story, 50,000-square-foot facility that houses its manufacturing, engineering, and inventory operations.

The firm designs and manufactures high-reliability discrete semiconductor devices, including transient voltage suppressors, rectifiers, switching transistors, Zener diodes, field-effect transistors, unijunction transistors, bridge rectifiers, and European-type equivalents. It also produces custom replacements and supports end-of-life device requirements. The facility maintains an extensive inventory to support same-day and short-lead-time shipments.

Its customer base spans military, avionics, industrial, and commercial markets worldwide. The company serves engineers and manufacturers who require stable supply, responsive technical support, and components built for demanding real-world conditions.

New Jersey Semiconductor differentiates itself through a library of both current-production and obsolete devices, a just-in-time delivery program, and on-site engineering support that helps customers select and qualify parts for critical applications.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Discrete semiconductor manufacturing", "Custom semiconductor replacements", "End-of-life device production", "Just-in-time delivery", "Engineering and technical support"], "industries": ["Military", "Avionics", "Industrial", "Commercial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping on stocked items; short lead times on most items", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Library of current-production and end-of-life devices", "Just-in-time delivery program", "Same-day shipping on stocked items", "On-site engineering and technical support", "50,000 sq ft facility with extensive inventory"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1957 -> /about", "Headquartered in Springfield, NJ -> /about", "50,000 sq ft two-story facility -> /about", "Specializes in Zener diodes, rectifiers, FETs, TVS, unijunctions, bridges, European types -> /about", "Serves military, avionics, industrial, commercial markets worldwide -> /about", "Same-day and short lead time delivery on most items from extensive inventory -> /about", "Just-in-time delivery program -> /about", "On-site engineering and technical support -> /about", "Designs and manufactures high-reliability discrete semiconductor solutions -> /", "Custom replacements and end-of-life device support -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "designs and manufactures high-reliability discrete semiconductor solutions", "founded_year": "1957", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-jersey-semiconductor-products-inc' AND approved AN