UPDATE companies SET description='New Process Fibre Company, Inc. has operated from Greenwood, Delaware since its founding in 1927. The family-owned business began as a specialist in non-metallic stamping and die cutting, producing washers, spacers, gaskets, shims, and custom shapes for a range of customers.

The company manufactures custom washers and components from a wide array of plastics and stamping materials, including Teflon/PTFE, nylon, vulcanized fibre, Lexan, phenolic, acetal (Delrin), G-10 FR4, Mylar, polyethylene, polypropylene, and UHMW. Its in-house capabilities cover non-metallic precision stamping, plastic extrusion, slitting, shearing, and die cutting, supported by a tool room equipped with wire EDM and CAD/CAM systems that allow the firm to build and maintain its own hard tooling.

New Process Fibre serves aerospace and military, appliances, automotive, electronics, HVAC, power tools, medical, and plumbing industries. Customers referenced by the company include Flotec, which uses its parts in oxygen manifold systems for tent hospitals; the University of Calgary; Knife & Gun Finishing Supplies; Tesla; Derby Fabricating Solutions; Mueller Die; and Klinger IGI.

The company emphasizes its vertically integrated “under one roof” model, highlighting that it extrudes its own thermoplastics and maintains tool designs for the life of a program at no extra charge. Management states that the family business remains committed to improving products, maximizing quality, and maintaining cost-effectiveness through hard tooling that enables tighter production tolerances.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Non-metallic stamping", "Plastic extrusion", "Slitting", "Shearing", "Die cutting", "Wire EDM tooling", "CAD/CAM", "Precision stamping", "Custom tooling fabrication", "Tool design maintenance"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Military", "Appliances", "Automotive", "Electronics", "HVAC", "Power Tools", "Medical", "Plumbing"], "materials": ["Teflon/PTFE", "Nylon", "Vulcanized Fibre", "Lexan", "Phenolic", "Acetal (Delrin)", "G-10 FR4", "Mylar", "Polyethylene", "Polypropylene", "UHMW"], "equipment": ["Wire EDM"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house tool room with wire EDM for custom tooling", "Extrusion of own thermoplastics", "Free tool design maintenance for life of program", "Hard tooling for tighter tolerances"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1927 -> db", "Headquarters Greenwood, Delaware -> db", "Family-owned -> page /", "ISO 9001:2015 certification -> page /", "RoHS compliance -> db", "Materials: Teflon/PTFE, Nylon, Vulcanized Fibre, Lexan, Phenolic, Acetal, G-10 FR4, Mylar, Polyethylene, Polypropylene, UHMW -> page /", "Processes: non-metallic stamping, plastic extrusion, slitting, shearing, die cutting, wire EDM tooling, CAD/CAM -> page /", "Industries: aerospace & military, appliances, automotive, electronics, HVAC, power tools, medical, plumbing -> page /", "Customers: Flotec, University of Calgary, Knife & Gun Finishing Supplies, Tesla, Derby Fabricating Solutions, Mueller Die, Klinger IGI -> page /", "In-house tool room with wire EDM -> page /", "Extrusion of own thermoplastics -> page /", "Free tool design maintenance for life of program -> page /", "Hard tooling for tighter tolerances -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "New Process Fibre has been Stamping and Die Cutting Non-Metallic Washers, Spacers, Gaskets, Shims and many other Custom Shapes for a variety of customers since 1927.", "founded_year": "1927", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-process-fibre-company-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New York Custom Interior Millwork Corp. operates from Astoria, New York, tracing its roots to 1972 when Teddy Lagos opened a retail wood workshop on Manhattan''s Fifth Avenue. The family-owned business expanded to a showroom and manufacturing plant in Long Island City before consolidating its current focus on high-end custom architectural woodwork. Today, Teddy''s daughter Elizabeth Lagos-Molinari leads the company, bringing a master''s degree in business and decades of hands-on experience to the operation.

The firm provides in-house design, fabrication, and installation for commercial and residential projects, running what it describes as a state-of-the-art facility capable of delivering all-in-one millwork solutions. Its scope covers sophisticated custom woodwork for interiors, with the capacity to handle complex finishes and materials beyond standard wood species. The shop serves as a single-source partner from concept through installation.

Clients include architects, interior designers, real estate developers, and construction management firms. Completed projects span stadiums, broadcast studios, luxury hotels, five-star restaurants, and high-end residential properties across the United States and internationally. The company''s portfolio reflects a concentration on premium commercial hospitality and entertainment venues alongside bespoke residential commissions.

The business was founded on a simple principle: create quality woodwork and treat people the way the founder would want to be treated. That ethos, described as a "Mom and Pop" approach to relationships, remains central to the company''s identity. Leadership emphasizes craftsmanship integrity, personalized service, and the combination of traditional values with modern production capabilities as the foundation for long-term client partnerships.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Architectural custom woodwork", "In-house design and engineering", "Millwork fabrication", "Finish carpentry and installation", "Commercial interior millwork", "Residential interior millwork", "Custom finish application", "Project management and coordination"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Hospitality and entertainment venues", "Luxury residential construction", "Architectural design services", "Real estate development"], "materials": ["Wood (various species)", "Custom finishes and specialty materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house design, fabrication, and installation under one roof", "Over 50 years of continuous family ownership and operation", "Established relationships with architects, designers, and developers", "State-of-the-art facility for complex custom millwork", "Single-source responsibility from concept to installation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 by Teddy Lagos -> /about", "Family-owned, Elizabeth Lagos-Molinari leadership -> /about", "Headquarters Astoria, New York -> /about, db", "In-house design, fabrication, installation -> /about", "State-of-the-art facility -> /about", "Serves architects, designers, developers, construction companies -> /about", "Projects in stadiums, studios, hotels, five-star restaurants globally -> /about", "Over 50 years in business -> /about", "Started as retail workshop on 5th Avenue Manhattan -> /about", "Expanded to Long Island City manufacturing plant -> /about", "Focus on high-end commercial and residential custom millwork -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We specialize in sophisticated and distinguished commercial and residential architectural custom woodwork... We offer in-house design, fabrications, all-in-one solutions", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='new-york-custom-interior-millwork-corp' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='New York Metal Fabricator operates from New York City, serving the five boroughs and surrounding areas. The locally owned and operated shop has been providing metal fabrication and welding services for over two decades, though a specific founding year is not published. No founder names are disclosed on the company''s website.

The company provides full-service custom metal fabrication, including structural steel fabrication (beams, columns, frames, trusses), architectural metalwork (facades, canopies, panels, artistic installations), custom railings and staircases (wrought iron, stainless steel, bronze), and NYC DOT-compliant outdoor dining structures for restaurants and bars. Its welding department offers MIG, TIG, and stick welding both in-shop and on-site via mobile units. Work is performed on steel, aluminum, copper, brass, bronze, wrought iron, and stainless steel, with capabilities spanning cutting, bending, welding, finishing, and installation. The shop follows a four-step process: consultation and design (including 3D modeling), fabrication, installation, and quality assurance.

Customers range from architects, designers, and property owners to homeowners and hospitality operators. The firm has delivered dozens of outdoor dining structures since the city legalized curbside dining in 2020, and regularly supports residential, commercial, and industrial construction projects throughout New York City.

