UPDATE companies SET description='Newonics is an electronics contract manufacturer headquartered in Salt Lake City, Utah.

The company provides a full suite of electronics manufacturing services, including surface-mount (SMT) and through-hole assembly, hand soldering, wave soldering, PCB layout and design, cable and wire harness fabrication, and quick-turn prototyping. It also offers conformal coating, rework, and in-house inspection capabilities such as automated optical inspection (AOI), X-ray, and endoscope inspection for complex components like BGAs and lead-free packages. Newonics works on both a turnkey basis, sourcing all materials, and a consigned basis, using customer-supplied parts.

Newonics serves customers across the electronics sector, from startups initiating new projects to established firms seeking a reliable manufacturing partner. The company encourages client involvement during first-article runs and testing to fine-tune production processes.

A stated differentiator is the company''s multi-layered inspection regimen: every assembly passes through three inspection stages, with AOI supplemented by X-ray and endoscope methods for components that are difficult to inspect optically. This focus on verification aims to identify issues before they reach the customer.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO9001','ROHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["SMT Assembly", "Thru Hole Assembly", "Hand Soldering", "Wave Soldering", "PCB Layout and Design", "Cable and Wire Harness Assembly", "AOI Inspection", "X-Ray Inspection", "Endoscope Inspection", "Quick-turn Prototypes", "Conformal Coating", "Rework"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quick-turn prototype service", "Turnkey and consigned manufacturing options", "In-house AOI, X-ray, and endoscope inspection", "Conformal coating and rework capabilities"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Salt Lake City, Utah -> db", "Services: SMT Assembly, Thru Hole, Hand Soldering, Wave Soldering, PCB Layout and Design, Cable and Wire Harness, AOI & X-Ray Inspection, Quick turn Prototypes, Conformal Coating, Rework -> /", "Certifications: ISO9001, ROHS -> db", "Contract manufacturing on turnkey and consigned basis -> /", "Company type: electronics contract manufacturer -> /", "Inspection processes: three inspection stages, AOI, X-ray, endoscope for BGAs and lead-free components -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Newonics is a Utah based electronics contract manufacturer.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='newonics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Newport Plastics LLC operates from Brea, California, where it was founded in 1976. The company has spent over five decades serving Southern California’s manufacturing base.

The shop specializes in custom injection molding using vertical and horizontal presses ranging from 30 to 500 tons, with barrel capacities of 1.5 to 10 ounces. It processes standard and engineering-grade resins, including thermoplastic elastomers and reinforced or filled polymers. In-house capabilities span CNC/EDM machining, stereolithography 3D printing, mold design and tooling, and Class 7 and 8 cleanroom production. Secondary operations include ultrasonic welding, pad printing, hot stamping, silk screening, assembly, decorating, packaging, and shipping. The company also provides engineering services such as prototype development, product design assistance, reliability analysis, material selection, and packaging design using AutoCAD and MasterCAM.

Newport Plastics serves the medical, telecommunications, aerospace, and consumer-products industries, as well as the promotional-products market. Customers range from OEMs requiring cleanroom-assembled medical components to brands seeking domestic alternatives to overseas promotional-item manufacturing.

