UPDATE companies SET description='Nimbletronics, LLC was founded in 2006 in Plano, Texas, by Chester Nguyen and Cuong Nguyen. Chester Nguyen, CEO, holds a BS in Computer Science with an electrical engineering concentration from the University of Texas at Austin and previously wrote test scripts for NVIDIA, Creative Labs, and Ixia. Cuong Nguyen brings 29-plus years of industry experience, including roles at Hitachi Semiconductor and Murata Manufacturing.

The company operates a humidity-controlled, 20-foot-ceiling facility in the 900-acre Research/Technology Crossroads district, running two SMT lines equipped with Juki pick-and-place machines (2050RE, 2060RE, 2050RL, 2060RL), EKRA and Juki G-Titan screen printers, and Heller 1809EXL reflow ovens with nitrogen capability. Nimbletronics specializes in quick-turn PCB assembly—supporting 01005/0201 components, 0.20 mm pitch placement, flip-chip, CSP, BGA, PoP, and leadless packages—along with through-hole, rework, clean/no-clean processes, and both RoHS and tin-lead soldering. Services extend to top-level mechanical assembly, cabling, flying-probe testing (via partner), turnkey solutions, DFM feedback, and layout design. Turnaround options range from same-day to 25 days for prototypes, revision re-spins, alpha/beta builds, and low-to-mid-volume production.

Nimbletronics serves engineers and OEMs across semiconductor, medical, telecommunications, defense, security, audio, video, industrial, energy, RF, and network markets.

The founders started Nimbletronics to create an environment focused on delivering on customer promises, citing a family-like culture that kept the team cohesive through three acquisitions. Their vision is to help engineers and OEMs realize designs quickly, and their mission emphasizes a dynamic environment for reliable on-time delivery with high quality.', certifications=ARRAY['RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Surface Mount Technology (SMT)", "Through-hole assembly", "Rework and repair", "Clean and no-clean processes", "RoHS (lead-free) and tin-lead soldering", "Quick-turn prototype assembly (same-day to 25 days)", "Low to mid-volume production", "Top-level mechanical assembly", "Cabling and wiring", "Flying probe testing (outsourced partner)", "Turnkey solutions", "DFM feedback", "Circuit board layout and design", "Panelization support", "Flex circuit assembly", "Rigid-flex circuit assembly", "Backplane assembly", "0.20 mm pitch placement", "01005/0201 component placement", "Flip chip and CSP/BGA/PoP placement", "Leadless package placement (QFN, DFN, etc.)", "X-ray inspection", "Selective soldering", "Conceptronics Freedom rework system"], "industries": ["Semiconductor", "Medical", "Telecommunications", "Defense", "Security", "Audio", "Video", "Industrial", "Energy", "Radio Frequency (RF)", "Network"], "materials": ["FR-4", "Flex circuits", "Rigid-flex circuits", "HASL", "ENIG", "OSP", "Immersion Silver", "Immersion Tin", "Lead-free solder", "Tin-lead solder"], "equipment": ["Juki G-Titan screen printer with 2D solder paste inspection", "Juki 2050RE pick and place (2 units)", "Juki 2060RE pick and place", "Juki TR6 Matrix Tray Changer", "Heller 1809EXL reflow oven (9 heating + 2 cooling zones, nitrogen)", "EKRA X5 screen printer with 2.5D solder paste inspection", "Juki 2050RL pick and place (2 units)", "Juki 2060RL pick and place", "Heller 1809EXL reflow oven (9 heating + 2 cooling zones)", "Conceptronics Freedom rework system", "Scienscope X-Scope2000 