UPDATE companies SET description='North Dakota Soybean Processors (NDSP) operates a soybean crushing facility in Casselton, North Dakota. The company was formed as a joint venture between CGB Enterprises, Inc., a private U.S. grain and transportation company with a 50-year history, and Minnesota Soybean Processors (MnSP). CGB Enterprises, through its subsidiary Consolidated Grain and Barge Co., operates a network of over 100 grain facilities across the Midwest and has run a soy-crushing plant in Mt. Vernon, Indiana, with a daily capacity exceeding 140,000 bushels since 1997. NDSP extends that processing footprint into the Red River Valley, giving local growers a year-round market for their soybeans.

The Casselton plant produces food-grade soybean oil, soybean meal, and soyhull pellets. The facility is described as state-of-the-art, designed to crush soybeans sourced from North Dakota and surrounding areas. NDSP offers producers a blended portfolio of pricing tools to manage risk and capture value.

NDSP serves the food, renewable fuel, and livestock feed industries. Its food-grade oil targets food manufacturers and the growing renewable diesel sector, while its meal supplies livestock producers. The company’s customer base includes soybean farmers in Cass County and the broader Red River Valley who deliver grain directly to the plant. Testimonials from state officials, county commissioners, and local farmers highlight the facility’s role in adding value to the regional agricultural economy.

NDSP states its mission is to sustainably produce and deliver high-quality soybean products for food and fuel markets while fostering a safe, supportive environment for employees, customers, and the community. Leadership emphasizes that local processing creates jobs, stimulates the economy, and provides farmers with more profitable harvest options. The venture was started to capture value from North Dakota soybeans within the state rather than shipping raw beans elsewhere.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Soybean crushing", "Food-grade soybean oil production", "Soybean meal production", "Soyhull pellet production", "Grain origination and procurement", "Producer pricing and risk management tools"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Renewable fuels", "Livestock feed", "Agriculture (soybean production)"], "materials": ["Soybeans", "Soybean oil", "Soybean meal", "Soyhulls"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Year-round local market for North Dakota soybeans", "Blended portfolio of pricing tools for producers", "Food-grade soybean oil for food and renewable fuel markets", "Soybean meal for livestock industry", "State-of-the-art crushing facility in Casselton"], "facts_used": ["Joint venture formed by CGB Enterprises, Inc. and Minnesota Soybean Processors -> /", "Located in Casselton, North Dakota -> /, db", "Produces soybean oil, soybean meal, and soyhull pellets -> /", "Offers blended portfolio of pricing tools for producers -> /", "Mission: sustainably produce high-quality soybean products for food and fuel markets -> /", "State-of-the-art soybean processing plant -> /", "Food grade soybean oil for food users and renewable fuel industry -> /", "Soybean meal for livestock industry -> /", "CGB Enterprises has 50-year history, operates over 100 grain facilities, soy-crushing facility in Mt. Vernon, IN with 140,000 bushels/day capacity since 1997 -> db", "Contact: ,  -> /", "Social: LinkedIn -> db"