UPDATE companies SET description='Northwest Communications Cooperative is a member-owned telecommunications cooperative headquartered in Ray, North Dakota. The cooperative serves communities across northwest North Dakota from its main office on Railroad Avenue and a secondary location in Williston. While the exact founding year is not publicly documented, the organization operates on a cooperative model, returning capital credits to its members and focusing on local service delivery.

The cooperative provides a suite of communications services including high-speed internet, landline and VoIP telephone (marketed as NCC iVoice), video entertainment through NCC Video+, and security monitoring for both residential and business customers. Operations are supported by a local technical team that handles installation, billing, and ongoing support such as remote troubleshooting and a customer portal for account management.

Customers range from individual households to small businesses and community institutions throughout the region. The cooperative’s service area emphasizes rural connectivity, and it participates in programs like the Foundation for Rural Service grant to support community development and education initiatives.

