UPDATE companies SET description='OMG Tooling Inc was founded in 1980 by Oliver Marino Gerardi in Oklahoma City, Oklahoma. Gerardi, known as the "original OMG," began by leasing a small space and operating a tool and die shop, sketching initial concepts on napkins before translating them into tooling and molds. His blend of art and science, combined with a passion for quality, established the company''s foundation.

The company provides full-service plastic injection molding, encompassing custom design, in-house tooling fabrication, and molding of plastic components. OMG maintains tooling capabilities that many molders have eliminated, allowing it to build advanced tooling, enhance existing molds, and manage transfer tooling from other suppliers. Its automated molding processes aim to deliver consistent quality at competitive production rates, positioning the firm as a domestic alternative to overseas sourcing.

OMG serves original equipment manufacturers across a range of sectors, including consumer goods, healthcare, sports and leisure, construction, transportation, infrastructure, electronics, technology, and industrial markets. The company highlights its ability to accept existing molds as transfer tooling, supporting customers who need to relocate production or extend tool life.

The firm emphasizes its U.S.-based manufacturing and central Oklahoma location as strategic supply-chain advantages, promoting "Made in USA" integrity and protection against intellectual property risks associated with global supply chains. Core values articulated by the founder—integrity, excellence, quality, dedication, loyalty, and customer service—are cited as the bedrock of its operations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic part design", "Tooling fabrication", "Plastic injection molding", "Transfer tooling management", "Tooling enhancement and refurbishment", "Automated molding operations", "Design for manufacturability advisory"], "industries": ["Consumer Goods", "Healthcare", "Sports & Leisure", "Construction", "Transportation", "Infrastructure", "Electronics", "Technology", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Various plastic materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house tooling design and fabrication", "Expertise in transfer tooling and mold refurbishment", "Domestic manufacturing with IP protection", "Central U.S. location for supply chain efficiency", "Automated molding for consistent quality"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1980 by Oliver Marino Gerardi -> /about-us", "Headquarters Oklahoma City, Oklahoma -> db", "Full-service plastic injection molding for OEMs -> /", "Services: custom design, tooling fabrication, plastic molding -> /", "In-house tooling capabilities, transfer tooling expertise -> /", "Industries served: Consumer Goods, Healthcare, Sports & Leisure, Construction, Transportation, Infrastructure, Electronics, Technology, Industrial -> /", "USA-based manufacturing, strategic central location -> /", "Values: integrity, excellence, quality, dedication, loyalty, customer service -> /about-us", "Automated molding processes -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "OMG provides full-service plastic injection molding for OEM manufacturers.", "founded_year": "1980", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='omg-tooling-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='OTHER Industries operates from Wilmington, Delaware, where it began over a decade ago as a basement operation printing shirts for the founders'' own clothing projects. The studio grew from those DIY roots into a full‑service apparel production facility, shaped by the graphic‑design and printmaking communities of nearby Philadelphia.

The company provides custom screen printing, embroidery, promotional‑product sourcing, and wholesale apparel manufacturing. All production is kept in‑house at the Wilmington location, where experienced printers handle artwork review, screen setup, printing, and quality control. The shop works with plastisol, water‑based, and discharge inks, offers Pantone color matching, and runs specialty inks such as puff, glow‑in‑the‑dark, metallic, reflective, glitter, suede, plush, high‑density, texture, and stretch formulations. Orders start at 24 pieces for screen printing and scale from small‑batch runs to large wholesale volumes.

Clients span clothing brands, restaurants and coffee shops, construction and trade firms, schools and universities, corporate organizations, artists and bands, festivals and live‑event producers, nonprofits, breweries and hospitality groups, and retail merchandise programs. The studio decorates a wide range of garments including T‑shirts, hoodies, long‑sleeve shirts, tanks, athletic and performance wear, work shirts, safety apparel, polos, tote bags, aprons, jackets, sweatpants, and shorts.

The founders chose the name OTHER Industries to signal a departure from traditional print shops, aiming for a studio more connected to design, music, and independent brand culture. Their approach balances design awareness, technical experience, and hands‑on craftsmanship, with a dedicated sales representative guiding each order from garment selection through finished delivery.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Screen printing", "Embroidery", "Promotional product sourcing", "Wholesale apparel manufacturing", "Artwork preparation and digital proofing", "Garment selection consulting", "Pantone color matching", "Plastisol ink printing", "Water\u2011based ink printing", "Discharge ink printing", "Specialty ink printing (puff, glow\u2011in\u2011the\u2011dark, metallic, reflective, glitter, suede, plush, high\u2011density, texture, stretch)"], "industries": ["Clothing brands", "Restaurants and coffee shops", "Construction and trade companies", "Schools and universities", "Corporate organizations", "Artists and bands", "Festivals and live events", "Nonprofits and community organizations", "Breweries and hospitality groups", "Retail merchandise programs"], "materials": ["100% Cotton", "50/50 Cotton/Polyester blends", "Performance fabrics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Small batch to large scale wholesale production; minimum 24 pieces for screen printing", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In\u2011house production by Wilmington\u2011based team", "Dedicated sales representative for each order", "Full\u2011service shop: sourcing, decoration, finishing, sewing", "No outsourced production or automated sales systems", "Technical expertise in artwork, materials, and ink systems"], "facts_used": ["Wilmington, Delaware location -> db", "Started in basement printing shirts for own clothing projects -> /about", "Evolved into full production studio -> /about", "Background in graphic design and printmaking influence from University of the Arts -> /about", "Name chosen to be different from traditional print shop -> /about", "Custom screen printing, embroidery, promo products, bulk wholesale apparel production -> db", "In-house production by Wilmington team -> /", "Dedicated sales rep -> /", "Full-service shop: sourcing, decoration, finishing, sewing -> /", "Screen printing specialty, bulk orders 24+ pieces, up to 7 colors -> /services", "Ink types: plastisol, water-based, discharge, Pantone matching, specialty inks -> /services", "Embroidery offered -> /", "Industries served list -> /services", "Garment types list -> /services", "No outsourced production, no automated sales systems -> /services", "Minimum 24 pieces for screen printing -> /services", "Small batch to large scale wholesale production -> /services", "100% Cotton required for discharge ink -> /services", "50/50 blend shirts possible for discharge -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "custom screen printing, embroidery, promo products and bulk wholesale apparel production", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "24 pieces", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='other-industries-custom-screen-printing-embroidery' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='OVERTAKE is based in St. Paul, Minnesota, and was founded in 2019 by Justin Grimm. After selling his previous automotive business to a private equity firm, Grimm observed that the original values of craftsmanship and community focus were eroding across the aftermarket sector. He established OVERTAKE to restore enthusiast-driven service and attention to detail for the Subaru community.

The company designs and manufactures performance parts for Subaru vehicles spanning WRX, STI, BRZ/86, Forester, Crosstrek, Impreza, Outback, Legacy, and Ascent models. Product lines include top-mount intercoolers, gasket sets for H6 engines, transmission mount inserts, post-MAF pipe kits, cam solenoid heat shields, and various accessories. Operations emphasize crowd-sourced development through a dedicated Facebook group where enthusiasts provide feedback before production.

The company supports contingency racing sponsorships and influencer partnerships, and maintains a dealer network for wholesale distribution. Hero discounts are offered to military personnel, teachers, and healthcare workers.

The founder states the business was started to counter a trend where corporate ownership prioritizes profit over passion. Differentiators include same-day shipping on orders placed by 2 p.m. CST, a 30-day return policy, free shipping on orders over $250 within the lower 48 states, and a pricing philosophy that aims to keep custom-engineered products accessible.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product design and engineering", "Crowd-sourced product development", "Same-day order fulfillment", "Dealer/wholesale distribution", "Contingency racing sponsorship", "Influencer sponsorship program", "Technical support and install guides", "Warranty service", "Customer service"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Subaru performance parts", "Motorsports/racing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping on orders placed by 2 p.m. CST", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day shipping on orders placed by 2 p.m. CST", "Crowd-sourced product development via community feedback group", "Free shipping on orders over $250 within the lower 48 states", "30-day hassle-free return policy", "Hero discounts for military, teachers, and healthcare workers"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2019 by Justin Grimm after selling previous company to private equity -> db description", "Headquartered in St Paul, Minnesota -> db hq_city/hq_state_label", "Manufactures Subaru performance parts (intercoolers, gaskets, transmission mounts, post-MAF pipes, heat shields) -> homepage product listings", "Serves WRX, STI, BRZ/86, Forester, Crosstrek, Impreza, Outback, Legacy, Ascent models -> homepage vehicle categories", "Crowd-sources product development via OVERTAKE Development Facebook group -> homepage ''Crowd-sourcing'' section", "Same-day shipping for orders by 2pm CST -> homepage ''Same-day shipping'' banner", "Free shipping on orders over $250 within lower 48 states -> homepage banner", "30-day return policy -> homepage ''hassle-fre