UPDATE companies SET description='OakTree Supply has served the Fort Wayne, Indiana woodworking community since 1998. Founded as a family-owned brick-and-mortar store, the business transitioned to new ownership in 2014 while retaining its family-operated character.

The company distributes a broad catalog of woodworking machinery, power tools, hand tools, and accessories. Its offerings include CNC routers and accessories from Laguna, Lamello, and Next Wave; cabinet and furniture hardware; jig and fixture hardware; sanding and finishing supplies such as epoxies, stains, and abrasives; and a range of professional machinery including table saws, band saws, jointers, planers, and edgebanders. OakTree also provides machinery consultation through its Industrial Machinery Specialist, Logan, and assists customers with business financing options.

The company supplies timber framing tools, dovetail and joinery equipment, and dust collection systems. Its marketing emphasizes serving both the “serious woodworker” and businesses looking to add or upgrade production machinery.

OakTree differentiates itself by maintaining a family-owned, small-business approach: every brand is researched and tested before being stocked, phone calls are answered by a live person without automated attendants, and free demo events cover topics such as turning, epoxy pouring, and finishing. Free shipping on orders over $45 and available financing further support its customer base.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Woodworking machinery sales (CNC routers, table saws, band saws, jointers, planers, edgebanders)", "Power tool and hand tool distribution", "CNC router accessory and tooling sales", "Cabinet and furniture hardware supply", "Jig and fixture hardware supply", "Sanding and finishing product distribution (abrasives, epoxies, stains, paints)", "Dust collection equipment sales", "Timber framing tool distribution", "Machinery selection consulting", "Business financing facilitation", "Product demonstration and training events"], "industries": ["Woodworking", "Cabinet making", "Furniture making", "CNC machining", "Timber framing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned small business that tests every brand before stocking", "Live phone support with no automated attendant", "Dedicated Industrial Machinery Specialist (Logan) for equipment consulting", "Easy business financing available for machinery purchases", "Free demo events for skills like turning, epoxy, and finishing"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1998 as a family-owned brick-and-mortar store in Fort Wayne, Indiana -> db", "Transitioned to new ownership in 2014 while remaining family-operated -> db", "Expanded into online retail to serve woodworkers nationally -> db", "Distributes woodworking machinery, power tools, hand tools, accessories, hardware, and finishing supplies -> /", "Carries brands including Laguna, Lamello, Next Wave, Festool, SawStop, BOW Products -> /", "Offers machinery consultation through Industrial Machinery Specialist Logan -> /", "Provides business financing for machinery purchases -> /", "Serves hobbyists, professional woodworkers, cabinet shops, furniture makers, and CNC operators -> /", "Differentiators: family-owned, tests every brand, live phone support, free demo events, free shipping over $45 -> /", "Headquarters: Fort Wayne, Indiana -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are a family-owned small business that knows woodworking. We''ve researched and tested all of the brands we carry to make sure you are presented with the highest quality products on the market.", "founded_year": "1998", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='oaktree-supply' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Oberlin Filter Company is based in Pewaukee, Wisconsin. The company states it has over 60 years of proven experience in pressure filtration, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed. Ownership details and founder names are not provided in the available information.

The company designs and manufactures pressure filtration systems that remove up to 99.99% of suspended solids from liquids down to 1 micron. Its product line includes the OLIMIN8R™ for single CNC machine coolant filtration, the Oberlin Hot Oil Filter for food‑processing frying and roasting operations, and a range of automatic pressure filters that operate at up to 40 PSI differential pressure. The filtration process forces contaminated fluid through filter media, traps particles, and automatically discharges a dry filter cake, eliminating wet sludge handling. The company reports serving more than 380 manufacturers, from Fortune 500 global operations to local machine shops.

Oberlin filters are used across a broad set of industries: industrial coolant systems (oil, water‑soluble emulsions, synthetics), metal finishing (phosphate bath recycling), food processing (frying and roasting oil), sulfur recovery, CNC machining, maritime scrubber systems, breweries and sludge dewatering, chemical processing, semiconductor and solar wastewater (silicon fines, gallium arsenide, heavy metals), crystallizer zero‑liquid‑discharge (ZLD) applications, and general industrial process wastewater treatment.

The company emphasizes that its differentiation lies in the dry‑cake discharge — turning waste into a handleable solid — which automates compliance, maximizes fluid recovery, and removes manual labor. It also highlights 40 PSI pressure force (four times gravity filtration), a typical 6‑ to 12‑month payback, and up to 80% reduction in filter media costs compared with alternative systems.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pressure filtration", "Coolant filtration", "Hot oil filtration", "Sulfur recovery filtration", "Maritime scrubber filtration", "Wastewater treatment", "Zero liquid discharge (ZLD) filtration", "Industrial process wastewater filtration", "Automatic dry cake discharge", "Filter media supply"], "industries": ["Industrial coolant systems", "Metal finishing", "Food processing (frying/roasting)", "Sulfur recovery", "CNC machining", "Maritime", "Breweries", "Chemical processing", "Semiconductor manufacturing", "Solar manufacturing", "Zero liquid discharge (ZLD)", "Industrial wastewater treatment"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["OLIMIN8R\u2122", "Oberlin Hot Oil Filter", "Oberlin Pressure Filter"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Removes up to 99.99% of solids down to 1 micron", "40 PSI pressure filtration (4X gravity filters)", "Automatic dry cake discharge eliminates wet sludge", "6\u201312 month typical ROI", "Up to 80% reduction in filter media costs"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Pewaukee, Wisconsin -> db", "60+ years proven experience -> /", "Removes 99.99% solids down to 1 micron -> /", "40 PSI pressure filtration -> /", "Automatic dry cake discharge -> /", "OLIMIN8R\u2122 for single CNC machine -> /", "Oberlin Hot Oil Filter for food processing -> /", "Industries: industrial coolants, metal finishing, food processing, sulfur recovery, CNC machining, maritime, breweries, chemical processing, semiconductor/solar, ZLD, industrial wastewater -> /", "380+ manufacturers served, Fortune 500 to local machine shops -> /", "6-12 month average payback -> /", "80% reduction in filter media costs -> /", "Equipment lasts 3-5x longer -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Oberlin Filters remove up to 99.99% of solids from liquids as small as 1 micron.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='oberlin-filter-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Occam Design, based in Louisville, Kentucky, was founded in 2006 as a division of CreoSalus, Inc. The company operates from two facilities in Louisville, including a main office on East Oak Street and a manufacturing facility on East Chestnut Street.

The firm provides end-to-end medical device development and cGMP manufacturing, covering project management, design for manufacturing, test development, production prototyping, regulatory compliance, and wellness/wearables device development. Its Louisville facilities house five Class 7 cleanrooms, a machine shop, and injection molding equipment, all within an FDA-registered, ISO 13485:2016-certified environment.

Occam serves clients across the U.S. and Europe, including medical device companies developing Class I, II, and III products, health-tech and wearables startups, equine device developers, and government-funded projects (NIH, DOD). Past clients include DeltaChase LLC, Trio Medical, Cerovations, MagnaWave, and a Fortune 1000 company, as well as universities such as Yale, Harvard, Duke, and the University of Louisville.

The company’s approach is guided by Occam’s Razor—“entities should not be multiplied unnecessarily”—emphasizing lean operations and a dedicated project manager who coordinates engineering, regulatory, and manufacturing resources. Occam highlights its ability to start or stop work dynamically, identify development and regulatory gaps, and maintain compliance with IEC 60601 and CISPR-11 standards for electro-medical equipment.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Project management", "3D animations", "Design for manufacturing (DFM)", "Test development and test strategy", "Production prototyping", "Wellness and wearables device development", "Regulatory compliance (FDA, ISO 13485)", "cGMP manufacturing", "Cleanroom manufacturing (Class 7)", "Injection molding", "Machine shop fabrication", "Market analysis", "Product development", "Quality and regulatory consulting", "Go-to-market strategy", "Distribution support"], "industries": ["Medical devices (Class I, II, III)", "Health technology", "Wearables", "Equine devices", "Government/defense (NIH, DOD funded)", "Academic/research institutions", "Direct-to-consumer health/lifestyle products"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Injection molding machines", "Machine shop equipment", "Class 7 cleanrooms"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 13485:2016 certified, FDA-registered facility with five Class 7 cleanrooms", "In-house machine shop and injection molding capability", "Dedicated project manager for lean, cost-controlled execution", "Experience with Class I\u2013III medical devices and IEC 60601/CISPR-11 compliance", "Government-funded project experience (NIH, DOD)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2006 -> db", "Headquarters Louisville, KY -> db, /, /about", "Division of CreoSalus, Inc. -> /, /about", "ISO 13485:2016 certified -> db, /, /about", "FDA registered -> /, /about", "5 Class 7 cleanrooms -> /, /about", "2 facilities -> /", "Capabilities list (project